    "closingDate": null,
    "jobDescription": "The Chief of Staff is the strategic execution partner to the India Country Manager, responsible for translating priorities into measurable outcomes. The role drives operating rhythm, cross-functional alignment, strategic initiatives, government affairs coordination, and leadership effectiveness across the India organization. As a trusted advisor to the Country Manager, the Chief of Staff enables decision-making, orchestrates high-impact initiatives, manages governance and execution mechanisms, and strengthens relationships across government, industry, academia, and internal stakeholders. Key Responsibilities\n1. Country Strategy &amp; Executive Support Focus: Enable the Country Manager to drive enterprise priorities and country-level strategic outcomes. Support development and execution of India country priorities and strategic initiatives Drive leadership alignment and OSIR review processes Provide structured analysis, insights, and recommendations for key decisions Develop executive communications, presentations, and briefing materials Ensure effective follow-through on leadership actions and commitments\n2. PMO &amp; Operational Excellence Focus: Drive execution discipline, governance, and organizational effectiveness. Lead strategic program and portfolio management across country initiatives Establish governance mechanisms and operating cadences Track progress, dependencies, risks, and action closure Drive accountability and execution across cross-functional stakeholders Improve processes, reporting, and operational effectiveness\n3. Government Affairs &amp; Ecosystem Engagement Focus: Strengthen NXP India's external influence and strategic partnerships. Support Government Affairs strategy and policy advocacy efforts Coordinate engagement with government, industry bodies, academia, and research institutions Manage ecosystem initiatives involving startups, universities, and innovation programs Develop briefing materials and stakeholder engagement plans Identify partnership opportunities that support NXP India's growth and reputation\n4. Stakeholder Management &amp; Organizational Impact Focus: Foster alignment, collaboration, and organizational effectiveness. Build strong relationships across business groups, functions, and external stakeholders Facilitate leadership forums, councils, and executive workshops Promote collaboration and alignment across the India organization Support culture, accountability, and continuous improvement initiatives Serve as a connector between leadership priorities and organizational execution Qualifications &amp; Experience Education Bachelor’s degree in engineering, Technology, Business, Public Policy, or a related field. MBA or equivalent postgraduate qualification preferred. Experience 10+ years of experience in strategy, program management, consulting, business operations, ecosystem development, government affairs, or leadership support roles. Experience managing cross-functional initiatives involving executive stakeholders. Exposure to technology, semiconductor, innovation ecosystems, startups, academia, or government collaboration programs is highly desirable. Key Skills &amp; Competencies Strategic planning and execution Program and portfolio management Executive stakeholder management Government affairs and ecosystem engagement Executive communication and storytelling Data-driven problem solving and decision support Cross-functional leadership and influence Governance, operating rhythm, and performance management Relationship building and collaboration Ability to navigate ambiguity and drive outcomes in a matrix organization Success Measures The successful candidate will be measured by: Effective execution of Country Manager priorities and strategic initiatives Timely closure of leadership actions, milestones, and commitments Quality of governance, operating rhythm, and executive reporting Strength of cross-functional alignment and stakeholder engagement Impact of government affairs and ecosystem initiatives Leadership satisfaction and organizational effectiveness improvements This position is designed to be a highly influential leadership enablement role, serving as both a strategic advisor and operational catalyst for India Country Management office. More information about NXP in India... #LI-9415 NXP Semiconductors N.V. (NASDAQ: NXPI) enables a smarter, safer, and more sustainable world through innovation. As the world leader in secure connectivity solutions for embedded applications, NXP is pushing boundaries in the automotive, industrial &amp; Io T, mobile, and communication infrastructure markets. For more information, visit www.nxp.com Bright Minds. Bright Futures. We believe that a key component to growing our business is to develop our people. To enable you to grow your career at NXP, we offer online and offline learning opportunities to help you develop some of your core and professional skills. Commitment At NXP. We recognize NXP is a powerful change agent as we continue to deliver innovative solutions that advance a more sustainable future. We remain steadfast in our commitment to sustainability and making measurable year-on-year progress. Also, we aim to create an inclusive work environment and we will not tolerate racism, discrimination or harassment of any kind. We have programs in place focused on diversity, inclusion and equality. Thank you for considering a career at NXP. To help you prepare for the different steps in our hiring process, see the following useful advice and tips. Are you already an NXP employee? Do not apply here. Instead, you must apply via our internal career page. Thank you for your interest in supporting our recruitment efforts. Please note that NXP operates under a strict Preferred Supplier List (PSL) for all recruitment activities. Any candidate profiles or resume submitted without a prior written agreement or explicit request from our Talent Acquisition team will be considered unsolicited. Such submissions will be deemed free of any obligations, and no fees will be paid by NXP or any of its affiliates, subsidiaries, or divisions\n- regardless of whether the candidate is hired, either coincidentally or otherwise. Thank you for your understanding.",
